## 2. Topic finding and research

**Sources (use 3+):** search autocomplete and Ask YouTube; outlier videos (far above their channel's average); Studio Research tab; competitor comments; Google Trends and Reddit; your own audience questions.

**Workflow**
1. Collect 30 raw ideas.
2. Search each and open the top 10 results; note dates, views, channel size, gaps.
3. Check demand lasts months, not a week.
4. Check small channels rank (a good sign).
5. Define your angle (better explanation, newer update, personal test, other level, other format).
6. Score and rank.

**Idea scorecard (1-5):** Demand, Competition gap, Your edge, Packaging potential, Series potential, Effort.

**Content pillars:** Search videos 40%, Browse videos (stories, opinions, comparisons) 30%, Series 20%, Shorts and community posts 10%. First 10 videos: lean to search-friendly questions.

