## 4. Video making

| Priority | Budget | Better |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Audio | Wired lavalier (about $15-30) | USB/XLR mic or wireless kit |
| Light | Window plus reflector | Key, fill, back light |
| Camera | Phone, 4K 30 fps | Mirrorless with fast lens |
| Stability | Phone tripod | Tripod with fluid head |
| Screen capture | Built-in/free recorder | Recorder with cursor highlight |

- **Audio:** soft quiet room, mic 15-20 cm away, peaks around -12 dB, record 10 s of room tone.
- **Light and frame:** key light about 45 degrees, simple background, eyes on upper third, 16:9 long-form, 9:16 Shorts, lock exposure and focus.
- **Workflow:** record the hook first (2-3 takes), shoot in chapters, pause 1 s between lines, 3-5 B-roll clips per chapter, record a spare hook for A/B, back up same day.
- **Faceless is fine if original:** own script and voice, visuals made per video, disclose realistic AI media, no AI hosts on sensitive topics.
- **Schedule:** Day 1 script, Day 2 record, Day 3 edit, Day 4 thumbnail/metadata/quality check, Day 5 upload and schedule.

