## 5. Editing and quality

1. Assemble and sync.
2. Rough cut (remove mistakes, pauses, filler).
3. Tighten the first 15 s.
4. Visual change every 5-10 s (cuts, zooms, B-roll, graphics).
5. Sound: clean voice, quiet music (15-20 dB below voice).
6. Accurate captions and key on-screen text.
7. Consistent color.
8. Watch once on phone and once on laptop.
9. Export.

**Audio target:** about -14 LUFS integrated, true peak below -1 dB.

| Setting | Long-form | Shorts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Format | MP4, H.264 | MP4, H.264 |
| Resolution | 1080p min, 4K if shot in 4K | 1080x1920 |
| Frame rate | as shot | 30 or 60 fps |
| Bitrate | about 8-12 Mbps (1080p), 35-45 (4K) | about 8-10 Mbps |
| Audio | AAC 48 kHz, 192-320 kbps | AAC 48 kHz |

Starting points to test, not official YouTube limits.

**Pre-upload checklist**
- [ ] First 15 s deliver the promise
- [ ] Clear, consistent voice
- [ ] No unlicensed music or clips
- [ ] Facts and numbers verified
- [ ] Captions checked
- [ ] Ending points to a specific next video
- [ ] AI disclosure set if realistic

