## 6. Thumbnails and titles

**Thumbnail rules:** one idea; 3 words or fewer; face or one large object; strong contrast; readable at about 150 px; consistent style; keep key items away from bottom-right; show something that is in the video. Size 1280x720.

**Title formulas (100 chars max, first 50-60 matter):** How to [result] in [time]; I tried [thing] for [time]; [number] mistakes beginners make; [A] vs [B]; Why does [surprising thing] happen. Honest beats clickbait.

**Test & Compare:** desktop Studio feature, up to 3 thumbnail or title variants, winner by watch time ([overview, third-party](https://vidanalyze.com/news/youtube-ab-testing-for-titles-thumbnails-2026-guide)). Test one variable at a time. If unavailable, swap manually every 2-4 weeks and watch CTR. Compare against your own average.

---

## 7. Description, tags, hashtags

**Description (5,000 chars):** lines 1-2 keyword plus benefit; one link; chapters (first at 00:00, at least 3, each 10 s+); 2-4 sentence summary that answers the question; resources; disclosures; 3-5 hashtags at the end.

**Hashtags:** 3-5 relevant; max 15 (more may be ignored); first 3 show above title; avoid #viral/#fyp ([guide](https://touhfa.art/blog/seo/youtube-hashtags-guide/)).

**Tags:** minimal role in 2026; 5-10 accurate tags, 500-character cap.

**Disclosures:** altered/synthetic content, paid promotion, made-for-kids.

