## 10. Analytics, monetization, growth plan

| Tier | Unlocks | Now (to 31 Jan 2027) | From 1 Feb 2027 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Tier 1 | Memberships, Super Chat/Thanks, Shopping, Creator Partnerships | 500 subs, 3 uploads in 90 days, 3,000 qualified hours or 3M Shorts views | Unchanged |
| Tier 2 | Ads and Premium revenue | 1,000 subs plus 4,000 hours or 10M Shorts views | 1,000 subs plus 8,000 hours (365 days) or 20M Shorts views (90 days) |
| Shorts revenue pool | Shorts ads/subscription share | No monthly minimum | 10M qualified Shorts views in last 90 days, monthly (includes existing partners) |

Also required: 2-Step Verification, advanced features, no active strikes, AdSense, eligible country. Hours and Shorts views never combine. Private, unlisted or deleted videos do not count.

**For a brand-new channel:** 4,000 hours before 31 Jan 2027 is unlikely. Target Tier 1 first and plan for the 8,000-hour bar. If close, apply early (review about a month, 30-day wait after a rejection; applications reaching YouTube by 23:59 UTC on 31 Jan use current rules). Existing partners must accept new terms in Studio by 31 Jan 2027.

**Income beyond ads:** affiliate, own products/services, memberships, Creator Partnerships, Shopping, new incentives for smaller channels (check Studio Earn tab).

**Monthly metrics:** CTR (Reach), average view duration and retention curve (Engagement), engaged views for Shorts (Advanced Mode), traffic sources, returning viewers, subscribers per video.

**Monthly review (60 min):** top and bottom 3 videos; what top ones share; where viewers drop; pick one change to test; update calendar.

**90-day plan**

| Phase | Weeks | Focus | Output |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Foundation | 1-2 | Niche, branding, setup, 30 ideas, first 3 videos | 3 videos banked |
| Launch | 3-6 | Weekly long video, 3-5 Shorts/week, reply to comments | 4-6 videos, 12+ Shorts |
| Learn | 7-10 | Analytics, double best formats, test thumbnails/titles, start series | Repeatable format |
| Scale | 11-13 | Collabs, series, community posts, lead magnet, apply for Tier 1 if eligible | 10+ videos |

**12 months:** M1-3 publish 12 long videos; M4-6 reach Tier 1 and launch an offer; M7-9 build a series and collaborate; M10-12 reach full-monetization thresholds and launch a first product or sponsor package.

**Mistakes to avoid:** changing niche constantly, reposting others' content or template videos, chasing unrelated trends, obsessing over tags instead of retention and packaging, buying views, misleading titles, quitting before 20-30 videos.

